{
  "company_name": "AeroParts Supply",
  "industry": "Aerospace",
  "use_case": "Aerospace aftermarket parts demand forecasting and backlog management",
  "space_title": "AeroParts Supply - Demand Forecasting & Backlog 📈",
  "space_description": "**Subindustry:** Aerospace\n\n**Use case:** Aftermarket Demand Forecasting & Backlog\n\nAeroParts Supply — aftermarket parts demand and backlog analytics across 20 aerospace SKUs and 5 customer segments (Airline, MRO, Military, OEM, Leasing). Demand Planners use this space to monitor forecast accuracy and bias; Aftermarket Program Managers use it to manage backlog aging and fill rates; the VP of Supply Chain uses it to size safety stock and defend lead-time commitments to customers.\n\n**Key KPIs**\n- Forecast accuracy / MAPE — aero aftermarket benchmark 20-30% (intermittent demand), <15% on rotables\n- Forecast bias (over- vs. under-forecast count)\n- Fill rate % (target >95% on AOG critical parts)\n- On-time delivery % (industry benchmark 90-95%)\n- Backlog value (USD) and aging buckets\n- Average lead time (days) by part category\n- Inventory turns (target 4-6x for aftermarket)\n- Total aftermarket revenue (USD)\n\n**Data sources**\n- `aftermarket_orders` — daily order line items with quantity, price, lead time, status\n- `demand_forecasts` — monthly forecast vs. actuals by part and customer segment with error %\n- `demand_kpi_monthly` — monthly summary with fill rate, backlog value, lead time, inventory turns",
  "schema_basename": "aerospace_demand_forecast",
  "tables": [
    {
      "table_name": "aftermarket_orders",
      "description": "Daily aftermarket spare parts orders with quantities, pricing, lead time, and fulfillment status.",
