  "metric_views": [
    {
      "view_name": "order_metrics",
      "source_table": "aftermarket_orders",
      "dimensions": [
        {
          "name": "order_date",
          "expr": "order_date"
        },
        {
          "name": "part_category",
          "expr": "part_category"
        },
        {
          "name": "customer_segment",
          "expr": "customer_segment"
        },
        {
          "name": "order_status",
          "expr": "order_status"
        }
      ],
      "measures": [
        {
          "name": "total_order_revenue",
          "expr": "SUM(order_quantity * unit_price_usd)",
          "comment": "Total order revenue in USD"
        },
        {
          "name": "total_backlog_units",
          "expr": "SUM(order_quantity) FILTER (WHERE order_status = 'Backlog')",
          "comment": "Total units in backlog"
        },
        {
          "name": "total_order_count",
          "expr": "COUNT(DISTINCT order_id)",
          "comment": "Total orders placed"
        },
        {
          "name": "avg_lead_time_days",
          "expr": "AVG(lead_time_days)",
          "comment": "Average quoted lead time"
        },
        {
          "name": "shipped_order_count",
          "expr": "COUNT(DISTINCT CASE WHEN order_status = 'Shipped' THEN order_id END)",
          "comment": "Number of shipped orders"
        },
        {
          "name": "max_order_quantity",
          "expr": "MAX(order_quantity)",
          "comment": "Maximum order quantity"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "view_name": "forecast_metrics",
      "source_table": "demand_forecasts",
      "dimensions": [
        {
          "name": "forecast_month",
          "expr": "forecast_month"
        },
        {
          "name": "part_category",
          "expr": "part_category"
        },
        {
          "name": "model_version",
          "expr": "model_version"
        }
      ],
      "measures": [
        {
          "name": "avg_forecast_error_pct",
          "expr": "AVG(forecast_error_pct)",
          "comment": "Average forecast error percentage"
        },
        {
          "name": "total_forecasted_units",
          "expr": "SUM(forecasted_units)",
          "comment": "Total forecasted demand units"
        },
        {
          "name": "total_actual_units",
          "expr": "SUM(actual_units)",
          "comment": "Total actual demand units"
        },
        {
          "name": "forecast_count",
          "expr": "COUNT(DISTINCT forecast_id)",
          "comment": "Number of forecast records"
        },
        {
          "name": "over_forecast_count",
          "expr": "COUNT(DISTINCT CASE WHEN forecasted_units > actual_units THEN forecast_id END)",
          "comment": "Records where forecast exceeded actuals"
        },
        {
          "name": "max_forecasted_units",
          "expr": "MAX(forecasted_units)",
          "comment": "Maximum forecasted units"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "genie_instructions": "DOMAIN CONTEXT\nThis space supports aftermarket demand forecasting for an aerospace parts distributor selling 20 SKUs across rotables, expendables, repairables, and consumables to 5 customer segments (Airline, MRO, Military, OEM, Leasing). Stakeholders include Demand Planners (forecast accuracy, MAPE, bias), Aftermarket Program Managers (fill rate, backlog, lead time), and the VP of Supply Chain (revenue, OTD, working capital).\n\nMETRIC DEFINITIONS\n- Forecast error % = avg_forecast_error_pct; aero aftermarket benchmark 20-30% MAPE (intermittent demand)\n- Forecast bias = over_forecast_count vs. (forecast_count - over_forecast_count)\n- Fill rate (target >95%) = on health_monthly fill_rate_pct\n- On-time delivery % (target 90-95%)\n- Backlog units = total_backlog_units from order_metrics where order_status = 'Backlog'\n- Lead time benchmark: rotables 21-45 days, expendables 14-30 days, AOG <24h ship\n- Inventory turns target 4-6x; below 2x indicates obsolescence risk\n- Total aftermarket revenue = total_order_revenue\n\nQUERY GUIDANCE\n- ALWAYS prefer metric views with MEASURE() syntax for aggregations.\n  - order_metrics (source: aftermarket_orders) — dims: order_date, part_category, customer_segment, order_status; measures: total_order_revenue, total_backlog_units, total_order_count, avg_lead_time_days, shipped_order_count, max_order_quantity.\n  - forecast_metrics (source: demand_forecasts) — dims: forecast_month, part_category, model_version; measures: avg_forecast_error_pct, total_forecasted_units, total_actual_units, forecast_count, over_forecast_count, max_forecasted_units.\n- Use GROUP BY ALL with MEASURE() queries.\n- For monthly trends, always wrap the date in DATE_TRUNC('month', <date_col>).\n- For \"Top X\" requests, return LIMIT 10 unless the user specifies otherwise.\n- Query base tables directly only when needing columns not exposed by metric views (e.g. part_number, part_name, unit_price_usd, fill_rate_pct, backlog_value_usd, inventory_turns).\n- When the user's phrasing matches a SQL snippet display name (filters, expressions, or measures), prefer that snippet.",
  "sample_questions": [
    "Top 10 parts by total backlog units — and which customer segments do they ship to?",
    "Show monthly trend in average forecast error % by part category over the trailing 12 months.",
    "Which customer segments drive the most aftermarket revenue this year?",
    "Top 10 parts by total order revenue — what is their average lead time?",
    "How has on-time delivery % trended month-over-month by part category?",
    "Which part categories show forecast over-forecast bias, and by how much?",
    "Show the monthly trend in total shipped order count across the network."
